abstract: |-
  yaml2script is a Python tool that extracts shell scripts from a GitLab CI/CD configuration file (.gitlab-ci.yml) and enables their testing, analysis, and validation with any command-line tool of your choice. It correctly handles YAML anchors, `extends`, and complex script structures, making it ideal for ensuring the quality, security, and correctness of CI/CD pipelines. The tool is particularly useful for automating code quality checks, security audits, and workflow validation in DevOps environments.
